<title>JAPAN: Sony shares fall, drag down Tokyo Nikkei.</title>
<headline>Sony shares fall, drag down Tokyo Nikkei.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Sony Corp sagged in late afternoon Tokyo trading on Tuesday, helping spur profit-taking in other blue-chip shares, traders said.</p>
<p>Profit-taking dragged down the benchmark Nikkei 225 index by 156.81 points or 0.82 percent to 18,884.29 as of 0550 GMT.</p>
<p>Shares in the Japanese electronics giant are regarded as a benchmark for Japan's blue-chip shares, which had attracted investors on the back of the weakness of the yen.</p>
<p>As of 0550 GMT, Sony shares were down 600 yen at 10,900 yen.</p>
</text>
